# doppler extension — InDusk-level env auth (gitignored once copied to .env)
#
# This file is the TEMPLATE. Copy it to `.env` in the same directory and fill
# in the real values:
#
#   cp .indusk/extensions/doppler/.env.example .indusk/extensions/doppler/.env
#
# The `.env` you create is gitignored and lives at the InDusk level (the
# workbench root in a worktree workbench), so a single token is shared by the
# trunk and EVERY worktree. `indusk worktree create` reads this token and
# auto-provisions each new worktree's env non-interactively — no per-worktree
# auth, no `doppler login` OAuth.
#
# Onboarding a new/3rd-party dev: they request a token, drop it in this `.env`
# once, and from then on every worktree they create provisions its env on its own.

# --- Auth (required) ---
# A Doppler SERVICE TOKEN (not a personal login). Scope it to the configs this
# project needs — for local dev, read-access to the non-secret `loc_*` configs
# is enough; prod/secret configs are managed separately.
# Create one: Doppler dashboard > project > config > Access > Service Tokens.
DOPPLER_TOKEN=

# The Doppler project these configs live under (e.g. "numero", "dusk").
DOPPLER_PROJECT=

# --- Config naming (reference) ---
# env-pull resolves per-app configs as `<prefix>_<app>`, where prefix is the
# profile: loc (local dev), stg (staging), prd (production). One leaf config per
# app under apps/*/, inheriting from the env parent which inherits from `base`:
#
#   <project>/base                ← cross-env defaults
#     ├─ <project>/loc            ← local overrides
#     │   ├─ <project>/loc_<app>  ← per-app leaf
#     │   └─ ...
#     ├─ <project>/stg
#     └─ <project>/prd
#
# `pnpm env:pull <profile>` writes apps/<app>/.env.<profile> (gitignored) for
# every app, pulling each app's `<prefix>_<app>` config.
